# Tutorials


## 1. SelfCheckGPT NLI – Hallucination Detection

* **Source:** Hugging Face Blog
* **Description:** A hands-on walkthrough demonstrating how to use SelfCheckGPT with Natural Language Inference (NLI) models to automatically identify potential hallucinations in language-model-generated text.
* **Link:** https://huggingface.co/blog/dhuynh95/automatic-hallucination-detection

## 2. XTREME – Multilingual Benchmark

* **Source:** Google Research
* **Description:** An accessible overview of the XTREME benchmark, which evaluates cross-lingual generalization across multiple languages and NLP tasks.
* **Link:** https://research.google/blog/xtreme-a-massively-multilingual-multi-task-benchmark-for-evaluating-cross-lingual-generalization/

## 3. NLLB-200 / FLORES-200

* **Source:** Meta AI
* **Description:** Provides background on Meta's No Language Left Behind (NLLB-200) project and the FLORES-200 evaluation benchmark, which supports research in multilingual machine translation across a large number of languages.
* **Link:** https://ai.meta.com/blog/nllb-200-high-quality-machine-translation/

## 4. RAGAS – Evaluation of RAG Systems

* **Source:** GitHub Gist
* **Description:** A practical implementation walkthrough for evaluating Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, including metrics such as faithfulness and consistency.
* **Link:** https://gist.github.com/donbr/a6e0fd539c1288b5ab3d88bb42f75a40

## 5. Belebele – Multilingual Reading Comprehension

* **Source:** Hugging Face Datasets
* **Dataset:** Belebele
* **Description:** A multilingual reading-comprehension benchmark available through the Hugging Face Datasets library. The dataset card provides dataset details, loading instructions, and licensing information.
* **Link:** https://huggingface.co/datasets/facebook/belebele

